\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.1}{\ignorespaces HM 0.7 is the most precise of the three admissible nets and the only one whose language respects the domain rules. Fitting visits and precision on the training log, all nets (left) and the most precise and fitting ones (right).}}{75}{figure.caption.34}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.2}{\ignorespaces Only IM 0.0, HM 0.7 and ILP 1.00 accept every frequent training sequence, while the filtered Inductive Miner nets reject the multi-block visits. Training sequences accepted by each sound candidate.}}{76}{figure.caption.35}%
\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6.3}{\ignorespaces The waiting time that ProSiT learns falls with the load of a block, while the observed delay rises. RMG blocks, training log, by the number of other stops in progress.}}{83}{figure.caption.37}%
